SCHEME / ROUTE DISCOVERY
-------------------------
apps/client/app.json -> "scheme": "sotto"
Routes found under apps/client/app/:
  app/index.tsx                -> gate: Redirect to /(tabs)/home if preferences.onboarded, else /onboarding
  app/onboarding/index.tsx     -> onboarding; has its own "already onboarded" redirect but is NOT the
                                   only gate — the (tabs) routes themselves have no onboarding guard.
  app/(tabs)/home.tsx           -> home tab ("For you")
  app/(tabs)/library.tsx        -> library tab
  app/(tabs)/vocabulary.tsx     -> vocabulary tab
  app/book/[bookId].tsx         -> book detail
  app/read/[bookId].tsx         -> reader
  app/reader/[bookId].tsx       -> (also exists; read/[bookId] is the one used by book detail's "Read" button per route naming)
  app/voice/[bookId].tsx        -> voice mode

Persistence: src/platform/persistence.native.ts uses `expo-sqlite/kv-store` (SQLite-backed KV),
NOT IndexedDB. No pre-seed hook was found for native (unlike apps/client/e2e/screenshots.mjs's
web IndexedDB seeding) — confirmed by reading persistence.native.ts and app/index.tsx. Native
onboarding was walked fresh via deep link, not seeded.

Sample book id used for deep links (from apps/client/dist/content/packs/fr-FR/books/):
  fr-chevre-de-m-seguin  ("La Chèvre de M. Seguin", Alphonse Daudet — matches the "For you" story
  shown after a fresh onboarding-bypass deep link, confirming the id was live/correct.)

BUILD
-----
$ cd apps/client && LANG=en_US.UTF-8 LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 npx expo run:ios --device "iPhone 17 Pro"
  (run in background, log: docs/evidence/build-attempt1.log)

Result: SUCCEEDED on the FIRST attempt. No fix/retry needed.
  - CocoaPods install: succeeded ("Installed CocoaPods")
  - xcodebuild: "Build Succeeded — 0 error(s), and 1 warning(s)"
    (warning: "ignoring duplicate libraries: '-lc++'" — benign linker warning, pre-existing)
  - Installed on iPhone 17 Pro, bundle id xyz.noelturlington.sotto
  - Opened via dev-client deep link:
    xyz.noelturlington.sotto://expo-development-client/?url=http%3A%2F%2F192.168.1.26%3A8081
  - Metro confirmed listening on :8081 (lsof -i :8081 showed the expo/node process LISTENing)

App launched automatically in the simulator as expected. First screenshot taken
(docs/screenshots/ios/01-launch-state.png) showed the HOME screen already ("Pour toi"/French UI),
not onboarding — the simulator's data container for this bundle id already existed from a prior
build/run on this same simulator (xcrun simctl listapps showed an existing Bundle/DataContainer
before this session's first boot), so onboarding state had persisted across the reinstall-by-build.
To capture true onboarding, the app was explicitly uninstalled and the already-built .app
reinstalled fresh (`xcrun simctl uninstall` + `xcrun simctl install` — both simulator-state
operations, no source files touched), then reopened via the same dev-client URL. This produced a
genuine first-launch onboarding screen (see screenshot 02).

INTERACTION METHOD
------------------
Method 1 — mcp__Claude_Code_iOS_Simulator__control (attach):
  Tried: control(action="attach", device="iPhone 17 Pro")
  Result: ERROR — "Xcode is installed but not selected. Run `sudo xcode-select -s
  /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer`..."
  This is the tool's own internal check (distinct from the shell's `xcode-select -p`, which
  already reported the correct path both before and during this session). The fix requires `sudo`
  and the user's password, which cannot be supplied in this non-interactive session. Per the
  task's instructions, this was not force-fixed — it was tried once, failed, and abandoned in favor
  of method 2.

Method 2 — xcrun simctl openurl deep links:
  Used successfully for every screen that is addressable by a route: onboarding (via fresh
  install + relaunch, not a deep link per se, but the natural first-launch route), home, book
  detail, reader, and vocabulary. This was the method that worked and was used for all
  screenshots below except the very first (natural launch).

  Key finding used to reach home/vocabulary despite onboarding not being completed by a tap:
  the onboarding gate lives only in app/index.tsx and app/onboarding/index.tsx (redirect if
  already onboarded); the (tabs) routes and book/reader routes have no onboarding guard of their
  own, so `sotto:///(tabs)/home`, `sotto:///book/<id>`, `sotto:///read/<id>`, and
  `sotto:///(tabs)/vocabulary` all navigate directly regardless of onboarding-completion state.

Method 3 — osascript/System Events UI scripting on the Simulator app window:
  NOT ATTEMPTED. Reasoning: this session is non-interactive/background — there is no live user
  available to grant the request_access / Full Control approval that computer-use-style tooling
  requires, and CLAUDE.md's own safety rule ("never type into a GUI window that could contain user
  content without confirming focus") plus the task's own instruction ("only if you have permission
  ... don't fight it, just note it") both counsel against blind-clicking the user's real desktop
  without a confirmed grant. Per the task's own allowance, method 3 was skipped since methods 1
  and 2 were both tried and 2 succeeded for everything reachable by route; only the two
  touch-only interactions (tap a word, tap Save) were left unreached, and those specifically need
  real touch/tap coordinates inside the WebView/text renderer, not a navigable route.

