SCREEN-BY-SCREEN: REACHED vs NOT REACHED
------------------------------------------
[REACHED] onboarding      - screenshot 02, via fresh install + natural first launch (dev-client URL)
[REACHED] home             - screenshot 03 (and 01/01b, stale-state variant), via deep link
[REACHED] book detail      - screenshot 04, via deep link `sotto:///book/fr-chevre-de-m-seguin`
[REACHED] reader           - screenshot 05, via deep link `sotto:///read/fr-chevre-de-m-seguin`
[NOT REACHED] tap a word to translate
    Reason: this is an in-page touch interaction on rendered story text inside the reader (no
    route/query-param exists to trigger a translation popup for a specific word). No interactive
    tap method was available: method 1 (native simulator control tool) failed on an xcode-select
    check that needs sudo/password we cannot supply; method 3 (blind AppleScript/System Events
    clicking) was not attempted for lack of a confirmable permission grant in this non-interactive
    session. Deep links (method 2) cannot address this because it is pure gesture state, not a route.
[NOT REACHED] save the word
    Reason: same as above — saving a translated word requires first tapping the word (blocked as
    above) and then tapping a "Save" affordance in the resulting popover/sheet. Neither step is
    reachable by URL.
[REACHED] vocabulary        - screenshot 06, via deep link `sotto:///(tabs)/vocabulary`; correctly
    shows the empty state since no word was saved (consistent with tap-translate/save being
    unreached, not a bug)

SUMMARY
-------
Build: SUCCEEDED on first try, no fix needed, no retry needed.
Interaction method that worked: xcrun simctl openurl deep links (method 2), for every
  route-addressable screen (onboarding via fresh natural launch, home, book detail, reader,
  vocabulary).
Interaction method that failed: mcp__Claude_Code_iOS_Simulator__control "attach" (method 1) —
  blocked on an internal xcode-select check requiring sudo, which needs interactive user auth
  not available in this session.
Interaction method not attempted: OS-level UI scripting / AppleScript (method 3) — no confirmable
  permission grant available in this non-interactive session; consistent with the task's own
  guidance to skip it when denied/unavailable rather than force it.
Not exercised: tap-to-translate and save-word, both pure touch gestures inside the reader with no
  deep-link equivalent.
No source files were modified. No files outside docs/screenshots/ios/** and docs/evidence/** were
written.
